From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: grammar-tax workbench <workbench@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:36:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] grammar : skip advance and recursion when no candidate matched

In llama_grammar_reject_candidates_for_stack, when no candidate matched the
char element on top of the stack, the next stacks were still built with
llama_grammar_advance_stack before the (empty) recursive call returned.
Return early instead. The result is the same: the recursive call returns
an empty list for empty candidates.

Applies on top of 0001 and 0002.
---
 src/llama-grammar.cpp |    4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/llama-grammar.cpp b/src/llama-grammar.cpp
index 4eaa2b9..b58f00c 100644
--- a/src/llama-grammar.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-grammar.cpp
@@ -1123,6 +1123,10 @@ llama_grammar_candidates llama_grammar_reject_candidates_for_stack(
         }
     }
 
+    if (next_candidates.empty()) {
+        return rejects;
+    }
+
     const auto * stack_pos_after = llama_grammar_match_char(stack_pos, 0).second;
 
     // update top of stack to next element, if any
-- 
